{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-333696" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5{e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe Wronskian of the vector-valued functions given above is $W({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066416/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc3ce6898e8f8dab9f9a179a0f257acf4954c5c5c4592c4f8f474f9ac025e99a"} {"question" "q-333696" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Wronskian $W({x}_{1},{x}_{2})$ of two vector-valued functions \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11}(t) \\\\ {x}_{21}(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{12}(t) \\\\ {x}_{22}(t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis defined as\n\n$$\nW({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=det({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=|\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11}(t) & {x}_{12}(t) \\\\ {x}_{21}(t) & {x}_{22}(t)\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Wronskian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W({x}_{1},{x}_{2}) & =|\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{3t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5{e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2{e}^{3t}\\cdot 5{e}^{-2t}-0\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =10{e}^{3t-2t} \\\\  & =10{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066416/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc3ce6898e8f8dab9f9a179a0f257acf4954c5c5c4592c4f8f474f9ac025e99a"} {"question" "q-333696" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066416/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6bdd60be2a2b463d1fbf9315ff535bfc3475f1261975508c62b026647a7c851e"} {"question" "q-333696" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066416/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc3ce6898e8f8dab9f9a179a0f257acf4954c5c5c4592c4f8f474f9ac025e99a"} {"question" "q-333696" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10e^t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066416/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc3ce6898e8f8dab9f9a179a0f257acf4954c5c5c4592c4f8f474f9ac025e99a"} {"question" "q-333728" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}t+1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}t-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe Wronskian of the vector-valued functions given above is $W({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066416/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc3ce6898e8f8dab9f9a179a0f257acf4954c5c5c4592c4f8f474f9ac025e99a"} {"question" "q-333728" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Wronskian $W({x}_{1},{x}_{2})$ of two vector-valued functions \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11}(t) \\\\ {x}_{21}(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{12}(t) \\\\ {x}_{22}(t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis defined as\n\n$$\nW({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=det({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=|\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11}(t) & {x}_{12}(t) \\\\ {x}_{21}(t) & {x}_{22}(t)\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Wronskian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W({x}_{1},{x}_{2}) & =|\\begin{aligned}t+1 & t-1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(t+1)\\cdot 2-(t-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2t+2-2t+2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066416/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc3ce6898e8f8dab9f9a179a0f257acf4954c5c5c4592c4f8f474f9ac025e99a"} {"question" "q-333728"