rence/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066416/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc3ce6898e8f8dab9f9a179a0f257acf4954c5c5c4592c4f8f474f9ac025e99a"} {"question" "q-322737" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{a(t),c(t)}"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066416/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc3ce6898e8f8dab9f9a179a0f257acf4954c5c5c4592c4f8f474f9ac025e99a"} {"question" "q-322737" "field" "field-5" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066416/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc3ce6898e8f8dab9f9a179a0f257acf4954c5c5c4592c4f8f474f9ac025e99a"} {"question" "q-322737" "field" "field-5" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "a,b"] ["math" "a,c"] ["math" "b,c"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066416/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc3ce6898e8f8dab9f9a179a0f257acf4954c5c5c4592c4f8f474f9ac025e99a"} {"question" "q-322737" "field" "field-5" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "a,c"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066416/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc3ce6898e8f8dab9f9a179a0f257acf4954c5c5c4592c4f8f474f9ac025e99a"} {"question" "q-322737" "field" "field-6" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066416/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc3ce6898e8f8dab9f9a179a0f257acf4954c5c5c4592c4f8f474f9ac025e99a"} {"question" "q-322737" "field" "field-6" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{e}^{t}"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5{e}^{-3t}"] ["math" "{e}^{-4t}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066416/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc3ce6898e8f8dab9f9a179a0f257acf4954c5c5c4592c4f8f474f9ac025e99a"} {"question" "q-322737" "field" "field-6" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5{e}^{-3t}"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066416/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc3ce6898e8f8dab9f9a179a0f257acf4954c5c5c4592c4f8f474f9ac025e99a"} {"question" "q-334527" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)-3{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs above, where $t\\in R.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.$\\,$ The function $a(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1-3t \\\\ 3t\\end{aligned}]$  \n{{field-1}}  \na solution of the system.\n\n$\\,$ The function $b(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2(1-3t) \\\\ 6t\\end{aligned}]$  \n{{field-2}}  \na solution of the system.\n\n$\\,$ The function $c(t)=[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ t\\end{aligned}]$  \n{{field-3}}  \na solution of the system.\n\n$\\,$ {{field-4}}  \ndoes not give a set of fundamental solutions to the system because the Wronskian  \n\n$$\nW({{field-5}})={{field-6}}\n$$\n\n$\\,$ for all $t\\in R.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066416/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc3ce6898e8f8dab9f9a179a0f257acf4954c5c5c4592c4f8f474f9ac025e99a"} {"question" "q-334527" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Wronskian $W({x}_{1},{x}_{2})$ of two vector-valued functions\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11}(t) \\\\ {x}_{21}(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{12}(t) \\\\ {x}_{22}(t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis defined as\n\n$$\nW({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=det({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=|\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11}(t) & {x}_{12}(t) \\\\ {x}_{21}(t) & {x}_{22}(t)\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- If the Wronskian is not identically zero, then ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are linearly independent.\n\n- If the Wronskian is identically zero, and it's known that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are solutions to the same system of linear ODEs, then ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are linearly dependent. In this case, they do **not** form a fundamental set of solutions.\n\nFirst, we write our system in matrix form:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}]x(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute the given vectors into the matrix differential equation:\n\n- $a(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1-3t \\\\ 3t\\end{aligned}]$ $\\text{is}$ a solution of the system. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}(1-3t)^{′} \\\\ (3t)^{′}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1-3t \\\\ 3t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3(1-3t)+(-3)\\cdot 3t \\\\ 3(1-3t)+3\\cdot 3t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $b(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2(1-3t) \\\\ 6t\\end{aligned}]$ $\\text{is}$ also a solution of the system. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}(2(1-3t))^{′} \\\\ (6t)^{′}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2(1-3t) \\\\ 6t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3\\cdot 2(1-3t)+(-3)\\cdot 6t \\\\ 3\\cdot 2(1-3t)+3\\cdot 6t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $c(t)=[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ t\\end{aligned}]$ $\\text{isn't}$ a solution of the system. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}(t)^{′} \\\\ (t)^{′}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3t+(-3)t \\\\ 3t+3t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-6t \\\\ 6t\\end{aligned}]\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, consider the set of solutions ${a,b}.$ Its Wronskian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(a,b) & =|\\begin{aligned}1-3t & 2(1-3t) \\\\ 3t & 6t\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(1-3t)\\cdot 6t-2(1-3t)\\cdot 3t \\\\  & =6t(1-3t)-6t(1-3t) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is zero for all $t\\in R.$ Thus, since $a$ and $b$ are both solutions of the same linear system, but their Wronskian is identically zero, they are linearly dependent and do **not** form a fundamental set of solutions of the system." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066416/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc3ce6898e8f8dab9f9a179a0f257acf4954c5c5c4592c4f8f474f9ac025e99a"} {"question" "q-334527" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066416/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6bdd60be2a2b463d1fbf9315ff535bfc3475f1261975508c62b026647a7c851e"} {"question" "q-334527" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066416/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc3ce6898e8f8dab9f9a179a0f257acf4954c5c5c4592c4f8f474f9ac025e99a"} {"question" "q-334527" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "is"] ["text" "isn't"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-